<script type="text/plain" id="promptSrc">ROLE
You are integrating the "HEX" mascot companion into my desktop app.

SOURCE OF TRUTH
The attached file `hex-mascot-kit.html` contains the complete mascot engine —
vanilla JS, zero dependencies, zero assets, one self-contained rAF loop.
The engine lives inside <script id="hex-engine"> between the banners:
  ═══ HEX ENGINE START ═══  ...  ═══ HEX ENGINE END ═══

WHAT TO DO
1) Extract that block VERBATIM into `src/companion/hex-mascot.js`.
   Do NOT refactor, rename, tree-shake, or retune internal constants —
   the spring values, easing curves and timings are hand-tuned.
2) Mount it:
      const hex = HexMascot.mount('#hex-host', { w: 240, h: 212, autoSleep: 60000 });
3) Drive him from my agent's event stream with this mapping:
      reasoning / planning tokens   -> hex.setState('thinking')
      tool: grep / search / read    -> hex.setState('searching')
      tool: write_file / edit/diff  -> hex.setState('coding')
      tool: bash / tests / build    -> hex.setState('working')
      task completed                -> hex.setState('done');  after 4s -> setState('idle')
      tool error / non-zero exit    -> hex.setState('error'); after 4s -> setState('idle')
   If several events arrive in the same tick, the LAST one wins (coalesce).
   After `autoSleep` ms idle he enters 'sleep' on his own; any setState wakes him.
4) PLACEMENT: <describe where — e.g. "bottom-right corner of the main window,
   floating over the editor">
5) EVENTS SOURCE: <describe how I receive agent events — e.g. "subscribe to
   window.agentEvents dispatched by my AgentRunner">

PUBLIC API — the ONLY things you may call
   HexMascot.mount(el|selector, {w,h,autoSleep,calm}) -> HexEngine
   hex.setState(s)   'idle'|'thinking'|'searching'|'coding'|'working'|'done'|'error'|'sleep'
   hex.setFace(k)    happy excited cool love wink surprised sad sleepy think neutral
   hex.say(text)     speech bubble + mouth flaps (emits 'say')
   hex.wave()        wave animation + chirp
   hex.hitTest(x,y)  true if the point is on the blob (Electron click-through)
   hex.on(evt, cb)   evt: 'state' | 'face' | 'say' | 'wave' | 'fps' | 'doze'
   hex.destroy()
   HexMascot.setSound(bool)   master mute for his synth blips

RULES
- Keep his physical interactions ON (drag, throw, poke, pet) — they are part of the design.
- The canvas is transparent; don't wrap him in an opaque card unless PLACEMENT demands it.
- Bubble + cursor styles are auto-injected by the engine — don't duplicate them.
- Respect my app's sound setting: call HexMascot.setSound(...) once at boot.
- If the OS reports prefers-reduced-motion, remount with { calm: true }.
- Optional: load "Bricolage Grotesque" + "IBM Plex Mono" for his exact bubble type;
  he falls back to system fonts otherwise.
- Never block the UI thread for him; he owns exactly one requestAnimationFrame loop.

ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA
- He renders and idles at ~60fps in PLACEMENT; no console errors; no network calls.
- Each agent phase shows its matching animation within ~100ms of the event.
- Drag + release springs him home; he bounces off host bounds and never escapes them.
- 'done' plays confetti + a check badge; 'error' plays a red flash + X eyes + shake.
</script>

